d register kernels are KEPT as backends (owner ruling, documented fragment, do not widen them), so rework those references so they lower from the projected semantic vector (derive/stack-image, derive/register-image over (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))); if a reference cannot be removed without a design decision, STOP and report it rather than inventing one. test_utils.cljc: resolved-of becomes derive over the projected vector. derive_test: the :old legs go out. Every test that builds a kernel through dl/adapt / rc/adapt (grep the 37 files incl. the 10 C4 files) switches to derive/stack-image / register-image over (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)). Keep coverage: nothing a deleted test pinned may silently vanish; list in the report every deleted deftest and where its fact lives now.\nDO NOT: touch the old kernel yin.vm.semantic, linearize, code (that is 8f); do the rename; edit docs; touch src/yang; regenerate goldens (8f); commit or stage.\nVerification, FOREGROUND only (never background a lane): `clj -M:kondo` on changed files with no unresolved namespace; JVM `clojure -M:test -n` for every changed test namespace; the whole yin.vm.* quick tier (see docs/agents/build-n-test.md); derive-test with `-e :slow`; debruijn/register_test and debruijn/stack_*_test; the changed C4 namespaces with `-e :slow`. Node/Dart lanes run by the orchestrator, not you.\nReport ./collab/<ms>-engineer-8e.report.md beginning with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID: file list, deleted-test ledger, exact commands and counts, any design question left open, truthful results (do not claim green unless you ran it). End READY or BLOCKED.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
