ster-hash r2)))))\n  (let [shared (assoc (app (v 'g) (lit 1)) :eid -90)]\n    (doseq [[a b] [[(lam '[x] (v 'x)) (assoc (lam '[x] (v 'x)) :macro? true)]\n                   [(app (v '+) shared shared) (app (v '+) (dissoc shared :eid) (dissoc shared :eid))]\n                   [(app (v '+) (lit 1)) (app (v '+) (assoc (lit 1) :tail? false))]]]\nRead 560 code files under src/ and test/.\nSubsystems: yin.vm\nclj: 77 namespaces\n   yin.vm-test\n   yin.vm.ast-walker-test\n   yin.vm.attach-image-test\n   yin.vm.cell-test\n   yin.vm.code-test\n   yin.vm.completion-test\n   yin.vm.continuation-invoke-test\n   yin.vm.data-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn-code-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn-register-effects-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn.register-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn.stack-effects-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn.stack-parity-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn.stack-tail-completion-test\n   yin.vm.debruijn.stack-test\n   yin.vm.effect-forgery-test\n   yin.vm.encoder-test\n   yin.vm.engine-gate-test\n   yin.vm.engine-test\n   yin.vm.ffi-test\n  \"The canonical register image's own bytes (design section 3): every\n   declared body's `[locals registers start end]` in body order, then\n   every pc-indexed tuple's bytes in pc order -- the two parts design\n   section 3's table names ('body ranges plus positional instructions').\"\n  [{:keys [bodies instructions]}]\n  (str (apply str (map encode-body bodies)) (encode-instructions instructions)))\n\n\n(def descriptor-hash\n  (jing/blake3 (debruijn-code/encode-scalar descriptor)))\n\n\n(defn register-hash\n  \"The ONE function that computes R (design section 3): `R = blake3\n   (register-descriptor-hash || canonical-register-vector)`. Received\n   register bytes must be hashed before decoding, as B1's wire rule\n   requires -- no receive path exists in this phase, but this function's\n   own shape (bytes in, hash out, no host-value peeking) already supports\n   that later use. R is a derived backend checks