{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > /tmp/8e/report-body.md <<'EOF'\n# 8e old lowerers out — uncommitted implementation, BLOCKED at C4\n\nWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p8e, branch srvm-phase8e. No staging or commit; Architect review remains required.\n\n## Result and decision required\n\nDeleted the three lowerer source namespaces and six requested test namespaces. Retained builders now project A with \"'`(:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))` and derive stack/register images. The register derivation returns the image itself; the stack derivation returns `:image` and `:side-table`. `test-utils/resolved-of` now caches derive/resolve over projected A. Removed all :old legs in derive-test and the unused resolved-tuples diagnostic reader from derive.cljc.\n\nThe two native kernels keep their executable behavior and supported fragment. Their old lowerer references were prose/refusal guidance, now corrected. The register format'\"'s stale lowerer commentary is updated. No backend capability was widened.\n\nSTOPPED under the prompt's design-decision instruction: \"'`yang.python.antlr.int-ops-test/nan-comparisons-test` and `float-division-edge-test` fail on both native backends. The mandated row-based `sr-linearize/project ast` throws `Semantic bytecode address collision` before native lowering. A minimal AST containing two separately boxed NaN literals reproduces it. The emitter produces the same printed NaN row/address twice, then rejects the pair. `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1214` compares prior/current rows with host `=` and `same-meta?`; NaN is not reflexively equal under that comparison. `semantic-register/linearize.cljc:217` routes the map AST through this emitter. This is not a native-kernel limitation.\n\nOwner/Architect decision needed: authorize a fix to the canonical row collision comparison preserving scalar/metadata identity rules, or explicitly approve the supported project-datoms entry instead of the prompt'\"'s project-ast path for affected builders. Neither change was made. Expected NaN behavior and Python outputs are retained; no claim of a green gate.\n\nThe broad quick run also encountered a sandbox loopback bind denial in unchanged \"'`yin.vm.linker.head-board-test/the-board-crosses-a-real-loopback-socket`. No final broad run outside the sandbox was attempted after the C4 stop. No approval review was requested or rejected.\n\n## Coverage retained and explicitly retired\n\n* All ten B0 contract deftests and their public result/error normalizer moved to debruijn-code-test. Consumers now require that namespace.\n* All nine R0 contract deftests moved to debruijn-register-code-test. Version 4 is compared with the actual source constant. Address laws use A/resolved A/derived images. The obsolete source=resolved-tuples and lift=to-named-semantics entries were explicitly dropped from the transcribed field list because those APIs retire; all other format facts remain.\n* Register format mutation tests (register bounds, jump bounds/scope, terminators, live shape/bounds/tail/exact, R2 operand kinds), resume CFG, and body-local liveness moved to debruijn-register-code-test.\n* Derive-test adds explicit scalar/free-name/shared-context expectations, native opcode vocabulary coverage, effect data-operand preservation, and the original benchmark workload values with run/step parity. Existing A-derived literal image/hash goldens remain unchanged. The deleted allocator'\"'s image/hash literals retire with that allocator; no goldens were regenerated.\n* Fetch/transfer parity now executes fetched H/R directly on the retained native kernels. Raw H/R-to-old-named-vector lift assertions retire; A is independently authoritative. No inverse was invented.\n* Register continuation tests select the non-tail call by its nonempty live set and check destination/live/captured registers against its instruction. Every defect mutation remains, without the deleted allocator's destination-3 assumption.\n* Native malformed-binder fixtures assert the projected-row entry's existing \"'`{:rule :slot-kind :path [1 1]}` refusal. Walker/old-semantic paths retain their non-symbol-parameter/kind expectations. Rejection behavior is preserved; native input now refuses earlier in row validation.\n* The 84-row ledger below identifies each deleted deftest, its surviving coverage, or its explicitly retired representation/lift/benchmark mechanics. No claimed performance threshold existed in the removed benchmark.\n\n## Scope audit\n\nNo edits to docs/, src/yang/, or src/cljc/yin/vm/{semantic,linearize,code}.cljc. Under test/yang/, only the ten authorized C4 files changed. No rename, golden regeneration, staging, or commit. Live requires/calls to deleted namespaces are gone; historical prose, archive files, and the production-pipeline audit'\"'s forbidden-namespace regex are not live dependencies.\n\n## Verification — foreground lanes, sequential\n\nAll reported logs are copied beside this report in its verification directory. Intermediate failures are not represented as final green evidence.\n\n1. Final lint: \"'`clj -M:kondo --lint $(git diff --name-only --diff-filter=AM -- '\"'*.clj' '*.cljc')\"'`\n   **0 errors, 0 warnings**. One informational unused excluded eval var in the retained stack kernel. Earlier mechanical require/helper errors were corrected.\n2. Initial focused command:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -n yin.vm.debruijn-code-test -n yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.register-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-parity-test -n yin.vm.debruijn.stack-effects-test -e :slow\n```\n\n   **151 tests, 7,185 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**. Before the final coverage additions. Native register/stack files have no slow-tagged deftests. Stack-tail-completion-test was also included in the later broad run.\n3. Coverage-port iteration:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -n yin.vm.